    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-033: Position Layout (relative + fixed)** - the smaller slice of the position feature set chosen after measuring what has visible impact.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (~80-120 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Why this scope, not the full position + :checked + :not + clip\n\nMeasurement decided it:\n\n| Feature | Uses | First-viewport impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| `position: relative` | 22 | **0 with real offsets** (all are context-only) |\n| `position: absolute` | 16 | 1 (search icon `top=50% left=9px`) - deferred to ADR-034 |\n| `position: fixed` | 3 | **0** (all target TOC toggle, not in first viewport) |\n| `position: sticky` | 2 | 0 - deferred |\n| `:checked` | 14 | 0 (all dropdowns/radios, none visible without click) |\n| `:not()` | 391 | ~1 (skip link, already worked around) |\n| `clip` | 3 | 0 without `:not()` |\n\n**Only `position` has real architectural importance for future work** (unlocks `z-index`, `absolute`, `sticky`). `:checked` / `:not()` / `clip` will be their own ADRs when the features they gate are built.\n\n## Honest scope call\n\n**This ADR produces near-zero visible delta on Wikipedia at desktop 1774.** The measurement confirms:\n- 0 fixed elements in the first viewport\n- All 22 relative rules have no offsets and behave identically to static\n- The 1 absolute element with real offsets (search icon) is deferred to ADR-034\n\nThe spec states this explicitly in three places. No overselling.\n\n## What ships\n\n### `position: relative` - no-op + context prep\n\nParse + store `Position::Relative` on `LayoutBox`. No layout change (block flow already works). Future absolute children can use it as their containing block.\n\n### `position: fixed` - out-of-flow + viewport anchor\n\n- Skip from parent's block flow (parent's `cursor_y` doesn't advance; parent height excludes fixed child)\n- Layout with viewport width as available content width\n- Position at `(top, left)` offsets from ComputedStyle, parsed against viewport\n- v1: `top`/`left` only (all 3 Wikipedia rules use `top:12px; left:12px`)\n- v1: no scroll interaction (anchored to initial viewport top-left; scrolling doesn't pin)\n\n### `absolute`, `sticky` - parsed but treated as `static`\n\nStore the correct enum value for future ADRs, layout as `static` in v1. Documented fallback. The search icon (`span.cdx-text-input__icon` with `top=50% left=9px`) renders in-flow at approximately correct position by accident; taking it out of flow without containing-block tracking would shift it unpredictably.\n\n## What's deferred (ADR-034+)\n\n- **`position: absolute`** - needs containing-block tracking. This is where the search icon gets proper positioning\n- **`position: sticky`**\n- **`z-index`**\n- **`right` / `bottom` offsets** (all Wikipedia rules use `top:left`)\n- **Scroll interaction for fixed**\n\n## Test plan\n\nImplementation will add 5-7 tests in `[layout][position][adr-033]`:\n- Each position enum value parses correctly\n- `fixed` without offsets at `(0, 0)`, out of parent flow\n- `fixed` with `top:12px; left:12px` at `(12, 12)`, out of parent flow\n- Following sibling after fixed child at normal flow position (not pushed down)\n- `relative` no-op (block flow unchanged)\n\n## Verification after implementation\n\nPNG renders **identical** to pre-ADR-033 (documented as honest zero-delta). The ADR establishes infrastructure for ADR-034 (absolute) to produce the visible change.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Scope split accepted** - relative + fixed only; absolute + sticky + z-index deferred to ADR-034+\n- [ ] **Near-zero visible delta acknowledged** - this ADR doesn't change the PNG; value is structural\n- [ ] **`absolute` treated as `static`** - conservative choice; search icon renders in-flow at approximately correct position by accident (deferring correct positioning to ADR-034)\n- [ ] **No `right`/`bottom` for fixed** - all Wikipedia fixed rules use `top:12px; left:12px`\n- [ ] **No scroll interaction for fixed** - anchors at layout time; scroll-aware positioning deferred\n\nRefs #174\n",
